<h2>Spec rules to know before you draw it</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Finished sides.</strong> Non-peninsula radius columns are finished on the <strong>face and 2 sides</strong>. Peninsula columns (RPBC) are finished on <strong>all 4 sides</strong> — use them where the back of the column is exposed.</li>
  <li><strong>Toe kick.</strong> Utility, base, and vanity columns come standard with a <strong>flush toe kick</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Wall heights.</strong> A "30″" wall column is actually <strong>30½″ tall</strong> — draw it that way so the bottom line matches the adjacent wall cabinets.</li>
  <li><strong>Vanity height.</strong> Vanity columns are standard <strong>30½″ tall</strong>. If you're using vanity-tall cabinets, you must specify it.</li>
  <li><strong>Depth limit on tall columns.</strong> Radius columns <strong>over 42″ tall</strong> have a maximum depth of <strong>30″</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Inset (Shiloh).</strong> Inset wall radius columns specified at 12″ (or 15″) deep are built <strong>13″ (or 16″) deep</strong> as standard.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Modifications</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Width:</strong> structural modifications are <strong>not available</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Height:</strong> structural modifications are available — pricing on spec book page C1.</li>
  <li><strong>Depth:</strong> may be <strong>reduced at no upcharge</strong>. Depth over the standard depth carries an upcharge.</li>
</ul>

