<p>These columns are new enough that some dealers haven't found them in their spec book yet. Keep this page handy, or ask your Pinnacle Sales rep for the PDF.</p>

<h2>Where to use it</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Island and peninsula ends</strong> — the most common place a hard corner gets bumped, and the most visible place to soften the room. The four-side-finished RPBC is built for exactly this.</li>
  <li><strong>Vanities</strong> — a radius end turns a standard vanity into a furniture piece.</li>
  <li><strong>The end of a wall run</strong> — a radius column on the last wall cabinet reads as intentional millwork, especially next to a window or open shelving.</li>
  <li><strong>Pantry and utility walls</strong> — RUC columns carry the curve the full height of a tall run.</li>
  <li><strong>Pairing:</strong> rounded ends and <a href="/playbook/pacifica-ventura-door-styles/">Pacifica's radius moulding</a> share the same soft-modern language.</li>
</ul>

<p>Need something the standard columns don't cover — a different radius, or a curved island end? Send a drawing through your rep. W.W. Wood will review it, and there's always a chance they can accommodate it.</p>

